# PROJECT.md

Copy this file to `PROJECT.md` at the repository root and replace every placeholder
line with facts about the project before using the flowkit skills.

## Project

Project name, one-sentence purpose, primary language and stack.
Top-level directory layout: where code, tests, docs, and scripts live.

## Status tracking

Where task and milestone state lives (file, board, or document) and the exact commands
that show and verify it. Skills that track status run only the commands listed here;
if this section has no commands, those skills skip the step.

## Git & PR

Base branch, branch naming convention, and commit message convention.
PR title/body template path, and any policy files that require a human operator
to review a change before merge.

## Checks

Every required check (test, lint, build) as a copy-pasteable command.
Exit-code discipline: a check that was not run is reported as `Not run`, never as passed.

## Docs map

Where plans, reports, decisions, specs, and design documents live in this repository.
Add one line per document type the skills should look up or update.

## Architecture rules

Path to this project's architecture law file, plus any hard module or layer boundaries.
State which files or directories must not be changed without special review.

## Quality rules

Code style, comment language, and formatting rules specific to this project.
Module boundaries and any project-specific constraints beyond the universal skill rules.

## PM hooks

Which planning skills apply here: write a spec before large or vague tasks, update
stakeholder-facing docs at milestones, run roadmap or sprint planning when asked.
Delete any line that does not apply to this project.
